      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fountain Park and Bandstand Park were named Great Places in Pennsylvania in 2017 for their historic charm and community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklinpa.gov/welcome",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the French and Indian War, the British erected Fort Franklin here in 1760, replacing the earlier French Fort Machault.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The oil boom of the late 19th century left Franklin with a well‑preserved Victorian downtown that still echoes its early prosperity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://franklinpa.gov/welcome",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Every October, Franklin hosts Applefest, a three‑day autumn festival that draws hundreds of thousands of visitors to its historic streets.",
